Package: GLOWpipeline
Type: Package
Title: Multi-Region Orchestration for GLOW Variant-Set Scans
Version: 0.1.1
Date: 2026-09-02
Authors@R: c(
    person("Ming", "Liu", email = "mliu5@wpi.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Hong", "Zhang", email = "consistencyzhang@gmail.com", role = "aut"),
    person("Zheyang", "Wu", email = "zheyangwu@wpi.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
    )
Description: Orchestration layer for genome-wide GLOW variant-set scans. Runs the
    GLOWr single-region test over a chunk's worth of regions under an output
    policy, splits a genome into array-task chunks, and aggregates per-chunk
    results into a genome-wide table with significance thresholding and
    overlapping-window locus merging. It is the counterpart of STAARpipeline in the
    GLOWpipeline -> GLOWr -> GFisher stack; it is cohort- and cluster-agnostic
    (resolved objects in, tables out) so a workflow script binds it to data.
URL: https://zwulab.github.io/GLOWpipeline/, https://github.com/ZWuLab/GLOWpipeline
